quick update about private prisons and  the federal government's use of private  prisons you remember that earlier this  year the Department of Justice made this  big announcement and it made bait major  major headlines a lot of people super  happy about it saying we are going to  phase out our use of private prisons for  federal prisoners now there were so many  ifs ands buts and caveats with this  thing that we spent like 10 minutes just  listing caveats for example most  prisoners are not held in federal  facilities they are held in state  facilities so it has no bearing on that  number two most prisoners are not held  in private prisons at all and that while  private prisons are inherently  ridiculous the idea that we would make  profitable the the idea of  rehabilitation of people who have  committed crimes most prisoners aren't  in private prisons anyway so oftentimes  how big of a problem that is is also  overstated however it's not going to  happen because when the first contracts  that were supposedly going to not be  renewed came up for renegotiation this  fall the Federal Bureau of Prisons the  Bo p very quietly decided to renew them  anyway even though the federal  government said they weren't going to be  in that decision along with the election  of President Donald mean that it is  pretty unlikely that the US is going to  see a reduction in private prison  operators anytime soon core civic also  known as CCA it's one of the largest uh  prison operators private prison  operators announced that hey we renewed  our contract with the Bo p and we're  gonna be running the McRae Correctional  Facility in Georgia for another two  years the only change to the agreement  since the last deal was that there would  be an eight percent reduction in inmate  beds obviously the ACLU is concerned uh  having a system where prisons look for  profits it's like having a fire  department that's looking for a profit  oh wait a second it's like having a  health care system that's looking for a  profit hey we have that and it makes  absolutely no sense not everything needs  to be profitable Pat I mean that yeah  that we can't seem to get Republicans to  understand that this was the glimmer of  hope I guess for phase  private presence in the end that's gone  away of course they're gonna cut things  like educational opportunities because  that would go against those prisoners  coming back to them and making more  money off of them no doubt about it and  when you look at it you know the private  prison federal deals I don't think I  have to restate my view which is it  would be great to eliminate those but  those are not the primary driver for the  problem we have with mass incarceration  I know you're probably sick of hearing  me say this by now but the war on drugs  we can't book begin to really solve the  incarceration issue until we deal with  the war on drugs cannabis legalization  is something that is going to help us do  that but think about all the money that  is tied up with the war on drugs we're  talking about everything from the drug  testing industry the alcohol industry  the private prison industry is part of  that addiction recovery law enforcement  civil forfeiture and asset seizure  seizures the DEA the ATF many people pat  don't get how many billions of dollars  are being made by all sorts of people  based on the war on drugs and its  funding police departments police  departments make a ton of money by  seizing assets in marijuana distribution  raids now they've got cars to sell  they've got cash in all sorts of assets  yeah I'm sure it's a multi-billion  dollar industry and the fact that it's  it to the detriment of people's human  rights is shameful its job it's shameful  is really the way to describe it and you  know I mean yes this is disappointing  that we are seeing some of these  contracts that supposedly were not going  to be renewed getting renewed at the  time I was careful not to overstate the  importance it was more symbolic than  anything else and listen if you're  looking for symbolic victories under  President Donald I anticipate that  they're going to be few and far between  make sure to give us a like on facebook  facebook live streams I've been doing  these three or four times a week I will  connect I will chat with viewers about  upcoming stories on the show take  questions etc make sure you like our  facebook page at facebook.com slash  david pakman show and you will be  notified when we go live on facebook
 

